    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Occupying an impressive site of approximately 0.17 acres, this wonderful home is tucked away in a peaceful cul-de-sac and enjoys an enviable outlook over a large green area to the front. Willsbrook is a small and established development, with only a limited number of detached homes, adding a welcome sense of privacy and exclusivity to this sought-after setting.\n\nBuilt in 1993 and extending to approximately 144 sq. m., No. 35 offers generous, well-proportioned accommodation with an excellent degree of versatility throughout. The property also benefits from a B-rated BER, making it a comfortable and practical home for modern family living.\n\nThe welcoming entrance hall leads to a bright and spacious ground floor comprising a generous living room and a versatile office/downstairs bedroom, sitting room/playroom, open-plan kitchen/dining room to the rear, utility, guest WC. Upstairs, there are four well-proportioned bedrooms, including a master with en-suite, along with a family bathroom.\n\nExternally, the property is equally impressive. The beautifully landscaped gardens feature a mature selection of trees, shrubs and planting, while a large patio area provides an ideal setting for outdoor dining and entertaining. The private rear garden is fully enclosed and not overlooked, offering a peaceful and secluded space with an excellent sense of privacy. The property enjoys a desirable South-West front facing aspect, 2 wooden garden sheds, while the sandstone cobble driveway provides off-street parking for two cars.\n\nFurther features include double-glazed windows throughout, zoned central heating and a recently replaced gas boiler.\n\nThe location is exceptional, with a wealth of amenities close at hand. University Hospital Limerick is just 500m away, making the property particularly appealing to healthcare professionals. The Crescent Shopping Centre is only 1.5km away, providing an extensive selection of retail, dining and leisure facilities. Families are exceptionally well catered for, with St. Nessan`s National School just 1.2km away and Crescent College Comprehensive approximately 2km away, both within easy reach. The property is also ideally positioned for access to Raheen Business Park, just 1km away and home to major employers including Dell, Regeneron and Analog Devices. The property is within easy reach of all major road networks and is just 4km from Limerick City.\n\nNo. 35 Willsbrook presents a rare opportunity to acquire a spacious detached family home on a substantial private site, in a mature and exceptionally convenient Dooradoyle location. With its generous accommodation, attractive gardens, excellent privacy and superb proximity to schools, employment centres and local amenities, this is a home that offers both comfort and considerable versatility for modern family living.\n\nEarly viewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate the space, setting and potential this exceptional property has to offer.\n\n\nEntrance Hall - 17'2 (5.23m) x 5'10 (1.78m)\nSolid timber floor, stairs and landing all Scandinavian Boen Oak , understairs storage\n\nSitting Room/ Playroom - 16'0 (4.88m) x 8'6 (2.59m)\nSolid timber floor Scandinavian Boen Oak\n\nLiving Room - 13'2 (4.01m) x 16'6 (5.03m)\nGas fire, solid timber floor Irish Oak, built in shelving, venetian style blinds, double doors to reception\n\nUtility - 8'5 (2.57m) x 5'7 (1.7m)\nBuilt in units, plumbed for washer/dryer, sink, tiled floor and side door to rear\n\nOpen Plan Kitchen/Dining Room - 18'9 (5.72m) x 14'3 (4.34m)\nModern fitted kitchen, sliding doors to patio area, tiled floor\n\nWC - 2'6 (0.76m) x 5'4 (1.63m)\nWC, WHB, Tiled floor\n\nOffice / Downstairs Bedroom - 9'11 (3.02m) x 14'2 (4.32m)\nSolid timber floor Scandinavian Boen Oak\n\nBedroom 1 - 8'5 (2.57m) x 12'0 (3.66m)\nSingle room with carpet, built in wardrobes\n\nBedroom 2 - Master - 10'5 (3.18m) x 13'11 (4.24m)\nDouble room with built in wardrobes, ensuite and carpet\n\nEnsuite - 5'5 (1.65m) x 6'8 (2.03m)\nWC, WHB, Shower, tiled floor and shower\n\nBedroom 3 - 10'0 (3.05m) x 6'9 (2.06m)\nDouble room with built in wardrobes, and carpet\n\nBedroom 4 - 9'1 (2.77m) x 12'6 (3.81m)\nDouble room with built in wardrobes and carpet\n\nMain Bathroom - 6'8 (2.03m) x 6'9 (2.06m)\nWC, WHB, Bath, Shower, built in storage, part tiled wall and tiled floor\n\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
      {
